From 0f9953c7ca1931da9db21a273f41088d3a89b11d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sebastian Matkovich <sebastian.matkovich@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 18:19:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] qcom_tlmm_sm6115: SM6115 TLMM GPIO and interrupt
 controller

GPIOs over the three register tiles, and the GPIO interrupts behind the
summary interrupt, after Linux's pinctrl-msm (level interrupts drop
RAW_STATUS_EN while masked, edge interrupts keep it). Pin functions stay
as the boot set them; gpio-reserved-ranges are never touched.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
